{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/775726-how-feirce-was-intertribal-war-in-premodern-times","id":775726,"title":"How feirce was intertribal war in premodern times?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-27T18:47:56-08:00","id":775726,"title":"How feirce was intertribal war in premodern times?","content":"ive heard various acounts across editions so tell me how feirce you think it was? an occasional flare up or nearly constant warfare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T20:19:21-08:00","id":775763,"title":"","content":"Real world primitive peoples engage in ongoing warfare against each other with far higher mortality rates than modern war albeit over a longer period of time. I take that as indicative as warfare among the Garou. Since Garou also have Rage, I'd expect it to be even worse. So put me down for the nearly constant warfare camp.<br /> <br /> To get an idea of what warfare was like for early man, you can read Jared Diamond's The World Until Yesterday. It has many salient aspects on tribal sociteies that I think would apply to Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:50:43-08:00","id":775799,"title":"","content":"The high casualty rates of early tribal cultures has far more to do with infections than actual kills in battle. Which doesn't really apply to Garou.<br /> <br /> I think it also depends on what counts as warfare. Garou settle things in less-than-lethal trials by combat. Is it warfare if two champions fight it out instead of Septs going full on battle at each other?<br /> <br /> I doubt full bore multiple packs against multiple packs with high death tolls were common. I expect threats of them were common, but generally solved with challenges instead of battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T00:42:39-08:00","id":775848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/775726-how-feirce-was-intertribal-war-in-premodern-times?p=775799#post775799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The high casualty rates of early tribal cultures has far more to do with infections than actual kills in battle. Which doesn't really apply to Garou.<br /> <br /> I think it also depends on what counts as warfare. Garou settle things in less-than-lethal trials by combat. Is it warfare if two champions fight it out instead of Septs going full on battle at each other?<br /> <br /> I doubt full bore multiple packs against multiple packs with high death tolls were common. I expect threats of them were common, but generally solved with challenges instead of battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put. I would consider that there may have been warfare over kinfolk and teritorry, and that the kinfolk would have taken the brunt of that conflict, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T01:52:32-08:00","id":775864,"title":"","content":"Most of the intertribal conflicts seem to concentrate around Caerns and the movement of kin. Garou and Kin seem to move together, be it Viking raiders or slaves being dispersed because of a failed revolt. When Garou move they attempt to seize Caerns in the new area, raising a Caern is a difficult and dangerous task. It is easier to seize an existing Caern. I also think that while such attacks happened the level of violence was not the exterminate on sight or Fenrir gather it is time to seize all of the land of the Fianna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:30:44-08:00","id":776138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/775726-how-feirce-was-intertribal-war-in-premodern-times?p=775799#post775799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The high casualty rates of early tribal cultures has far more to do with infections than actual kills in battle. Which doesn't really apply to Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death by infection doesn't explain why tribal societies had a far higher death rate than other pre-modern societies which had states. The reason for the higher death toll were:<br /> <br /> 1) Warfare is chronic. There is no state system in place that regulates warfare or provides protection.<br /> 2) Exterminating the enemy (massacring everyone) was the main goal of primitive war. States usually don't have that as a goal because a subdued enemy population can be used as slaves or as a tax base, but primitive societies can't exploit that. Furthermore, they don't take prisoners in battle either.<br /> 3) Revenge killings are the prominent factor in war. This produces an endless cycle.<br /> 4) Lack of central leadership. 90% of people can prefer not to go to war, but if the other 10% are hotheads there is little that can be done to subdue them,a nd the plunge the whole group into the next cycle of war.<br /> <br /> All of these things apply equally to the Garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Garou do have a common enemy in the Wyrm (and the other Fera at times), and they eventually built up a system that emphasized commonalities and tried to limit internal conflict. However, I think this applies far less the earlier back in time you go. Especially in the time before the Middle Ages, I think the Garou will have a lot of time to direct their aggression at each other because there are no obvious greater threats for many times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/775726-how-feirce-was-intertribal-war-in-premodern-times?p=775799#post775799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it also depends on what counts as warfare. Garou settle things in less-than-lethal trials by combat. Is it warfare if two champions fight it out instead of Septs going full on battle at each other?<br /> <br /> I doubt full bore multiple packs against multiple packs with high death tolls were common. I expect threats of them were common, but generally solved with challenges instead of battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this applies only within septs or perhaps allied septs that have much in common. I think conflicts between tribes would be quite bloody.<br /> <br /> There are always going to wars over scarce resources. I also don't see the Garou with their Rage doing a much better job than humans even with some of their cultural ways in resolving conflict.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:49:19-08:00","id":776154,"title":"","content":"I strongly agree with <b>Black Fox</b>'s view on it. Even the things the Garou do that could lessen the strife are also for <u>modern</u> Garou. Even if they are a considerable anachronic society, they are still an evolving one, and there are no reason to think they where less warlike than the humans around in other times.<br /> <br /> What I do think is that, though bloody, their warfare had less casualties than the human ones. But that is simply because the Garou are far tougher, and to exterminate the losers wouldn't be an option. Most of the time, they would live in fair numbers to come back for revenge...<br /> <br /> About disease, it really had a greater presence also because the main source of deaths in battles was the poor conditions to treat the injured, when they could be treated at all. But getting this out of the equation reduces the deaths, not the violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}